One commit should represent one coherent engineering decision.

Good examples:

```text
fix(governance): preserve metadata snapshot provenance
chore(ci): align npm toolchain with repository contract
chore(migration): enforce TypeScript freeze
docs(migration): inventory legacy TypeScript responsibilities
feat(events): implement canonical analytical producer in Python
test(events): prove Python-TypeScript producer parity
refactor(events): cut analytical event generation to Python
chore(events): remove retired TypeScript producer
```

Avoid:

```text
update stuff
fix project
AI changes
refactor many things
```

